        "question": "A 68-year-old man with heart failure (LVEF 30%) presents with poor sleep quality and daytime fatigue. Polysomnography reveals repetitive apnoeas with ABSENT respiratory effort, Cheyne-Stokes breathing pattern, and AHI of 28 events/hour. What is the MOST likely diagnosis?",
