        "question": "A 28-year-old man with Duchenne muscular dystrophy presents with morning headaches, daytime somnolence, and ankle oedema. Overnight oximetry shows sustained desaturations to 82% during sleep with normal daytime oxygen saturations. Spirometry shows FVC 1.2L (35% predicted). What is the MOST appropriate management?",
