        "id": "WEEK3_RESP_194",
        "question": "A 42-year-old non-smoker presents with a dry cough persisting for 12 weeks despite treatment with proton pump inhibitor and intranasal corticosteroids. She denies wheeze, dyspnoea, or postnasal drip. Chest X-ray is normal. What is the MOST appropriate next investigation?",
        "options": {
